<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia says two new oil wells come up dry.</title>
<headline>Colombia says two new oil wells come up dry.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state oil company Ecopetrol said two new exploratory wells perforated by Triton Eneregy Corp and Occidental Petroleum Corp in central Colombia had turned out dry.</p>
<p>A terse statement from Ecopetrol gave no details, saying only that Occidental's Tamauka well outside Bogota, and Triton's Yumeca Dos in the upper part of the Middle Magdalena Valley, had both failed to produce any sign of crude oil.</p>
<p>((-- Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
